      "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a site. Let <MATH_0002>\nbe a surjection of sheaves of rings. Assume given the following data\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> flat <MATH_0003>-modules <MATH_0004>,\n<STRUCT_0003> maps of <MATH_0005>-modules <MATH_0006>,\n<STRUCT_0004> a complex <MATH_0007> of <MATH_0008>-modules,\n<STRUCT_0005> maps of <MATH_0009>-modules <MATH_0010>\n<STRUCT_0006>\nsuch that\n<STRUCT_0007>\n<ITEMOPEN_0001>(a)<ITEMCLOSE_0001> <MATH_0011> for <MATH_0012>,\n<ITEMOPEN_0002>(b)<ITEMCLOSE_0002> <MATH_0013> for <MATH_0014>,\n<ITEMOPEN_0003>(c)<ITEMCLOSE_0003> with\n<MATH_0015>\nthe induced maps determine a complex <MATH_0016> and a map\nof complexes <MATH_0017>.\n<STRUCT_0008>\nThen there exist\n<STRUCT_0009>\n<STRUCT_0010>\nflat <MATH_0018>-modules <MATH_0019>,\n<STRUCT_0011>\nmaps of <MATH_0020>-modules <MATH_0021>,\n<STRUCT_0012>\nmaps of <MATH_0022>-modules <MATH_0023>,\n<STRUCT_0013>\nmaps of <MATH_0024>-modules <MATH_0025>,\n<STRUCT_0014>\nsuch that <MATH_0026> for <MATH_0027>, such that the diagrams\n<MATH_0028>\ncommute for all <MATH_0029>, such that the composition\n<MATH_0030>\nis the given map <MATH_0031>, and such that with\n<MATH_0032>\nwe obtain a complex <MATH_0033> and map of complexes\n<MATH_0034> which is a\nquasi-isomorphism.\n",
